CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786141095
OL,3,CMajor travel disruption continues for
OL,4,Crail passengers following power outage
OL,6,FEngineers are making "good progress"
OL,7,Ffixing signalling issues but there
OL,8,Fwill be cancellations for the rest of
OL,9,Fthe night, Network Rail said.
OL,11,FFurther disruption tomorrow is likely
OL,12,Fbecause many trains and their crew
OL,13,F"are not where they would normally be
OL,14,Fafter this unexpected incident", it
OL,15,Fadded.
OL,17,FChris Wright, Network Rail's North
OL,18,FWest route director, said: "I'm
OL,19,Fextremely sorry for the disruption
OL,20,Ftoday and the very difficult journeys
OL,21,Fmany people have experienced.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
